 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "SecondBrainSystem() starts empty. Times are passed in by the caller and never decrease across createNote, updateNote and revertNote calls. createNote(title, content, timestamp) returns the next id \"note1\", \"note2\", ... (ids are never reused). getNote(noteId) returns [title, content, createdAt, updatedAt] or [] when absent. updateNote(noteId, title, content, timestamp) replaces title and content, sets updatedAt and returns true, or returns false when absent. deleteNote(noteId) returns whether a note was removed. searchNotes(keyword) returns the ids of notes whose title or content contains keyword, ignoring ASCII case, ordered by updatedAt descending then by id number ascending. addTag(noteId, tag) returns false when the note is missing or already has the tag, otherwise adds it; removeTag(noteId, tag) returns whether the tag was removed; getNotesByTag(tag) returns the ids holding the tag by id number ascending. Tags do not change updatedAt and disappear with their note. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
